\section{Signed-network terms}{

The package provides native (C) ergm terms for signed networks, evaluated on
networks built by \code{\link[=as_signed_network]{as_signed_network()}}:
\link[=gwesf_pos-ergmTerm]{gwesf_pos}, \link[=gwesf_neg-ergmTerm]{gwesf_neg},
\link[=gwese_pos-ergmTerm]{gwese_pos}, \link[=gwese_neg-ergmTerm]{gwese_neg},
\link[=gwesp_signed-ergmTerm]{gwesp_signed}, \link[=esp_signed-ergmTerm]{esp_signed},
\link[=gwdegree_neg-ergmTerm]{gwdegree_neg}, \link[=degree_neg-ergmTerm]{degree_neg} and
\link[=triangle_signed-ergmTerm]{triangle_signed}, together with the sample space
constraint \link[=active_signs-ergmConstraint]{active_signs}. Any other ergm term
(e.g. \code{edges}, \code{nodematch()}, \code{gwdegree()}, \code{gwesp()}) applies to the
positive ties. Models written with the multilayer terms of
\pkg{ergm.multi} (\code{L()}, \code{gwespL()}, ...) are also supported.
